 "e": 55.8, "t": "Ceres is tiny. The next world is bigger, and it has a heart you could see from your backyard.", "w": [["ceres", 50.53], ["is", 51.1], ["tiny", 51.37], ["the", 52.23], ["next", 52.32], ["world", 52.6], ["is", 52.87], ["bigger", 52.99], ["and", 53.59], ["it", 53.7], ["has", 53.79], ["a", 53.96], ["heart", 54.01], ["you", 54.35], ["could", 54.46], ["see", 54.57], ["from", 54.84], ["your", 54.99], ["backyard", 55.11]]}, {"s": 56.21, "e": 64.64, "t": "Pluto. About two thirds as wide as the Moon, but far brighter, because it's covered in ice. A full Pluto would shine about twice as bright as a full Moon.", "w": [["pluto", 56.21], ["about", 57.01], ["two", 57.27], ["thirds", 57.55], ["as", 57.9], ["wide", 58.01], ["as", 58.28], ["the", 58.39], ["moon", 58.46], ["but", 58.87], ["far", 59.0], ["brighter", 59.46], ["because", 59.88], ["it's", 60.15], ["covered", 60.28], ["in", 60.63], ["ice", 60.78], ["a", 61.46], ["full", 61.5], ["pluto", 61.86], ["would", 62.23], ["shine", 62.36], ["about", 62.66], ["twice", 62.9], ["as", 63.35], ["bright", 63.46], ["as", 63.79], ["a", 63.9], ["full", 63.94], ["moon", 64.29]]}, {"s": 64.91, "e": 72.37, "t": "And on it, a giant glacier shaped like a heart, about a thousand kilometers wide. From Earth, you could see that heart with your own eyes.", "w": [["and", 64.91], ["on", 65.03], ["it", 65.24], ["a", 65.66], ["giant", 65.72], ["glacier", 66.22], ["shaped", 66.68], ["like", 67.03], ["a", 67.16], ["heart", 67.21], ["about", 67.83], ["a", 68.02], ["thousand", 68.06], ["kilometers", 68.61], ["wide", 69.14], ["from", 69.79], ["earth", 69.95], ["you", 70.54], ["could", 70.65], ["see", 70.77], ["that", 71.04], ["heart", 71.23], ["with", 71.44], ["your", 71.57], ["own", 71.73], ["eyes", 71.97]]}, {"s": 72.63, "e": 78.57, "t": "Its pull on the oceans would be only about a fifth of the Moon's. Gentle tides. A beautiful, quiet sky.", "w": [["its", 72.63], ["pull", 72.79], ["on", 73.03], ["the", 73.13], ["oceans", 73.26], ["would", 73.67], ["be", 73.78], ["only", 73.95], ["about", 74.23], ["a", 74.43], ["fifth", 74.47], ["of", 74.9], ["the", 75.0], ["moon's", 75.06], ["gentle", 75.78], ["tides", 76.15], ["a", 76.95], ["beautiful", 77.0], ["quiet", 77.67], ["sky", 78.17]]}, {"s": 79.02, "e": 84.25, "t": "Pluto lost its title of planet in 2006. The next one is the smallest real planet.", "w": [["pluto", 79.02], ["lost", 79.32], ["its", 79.65], ["title", 79.79], ["of", 80.1], ["planet", 80.18], ["in", 80.66], ["the", 80.77], ["next", 81.19], ["one", 81.4], ["is", 81.59], ["the", 81.95], ["smallest", 82.26], ["real", 83.56], ["planet", 83.81]]}, {"s": 84.65, "e": 92.35, "t": "Mercury. The smallest planet. It's only about a third wider than our Moon, and it looks a lot like it. Grey, cratered, no air.", "w": [["mercury", 84.65], ["the", 85.5], ["smallest", 85.58], ["planet", 86.23], ["it's", 86.92], ["only", 87.06], ["about", 87.28], ["a", 87.49], ["third", 87.53], ["wider", 87.92], ["than", 88.29], ["our", 88.42], ["moon", 88.53], ["and", 89.06], ["it", 89.15], ["looks", 89.23], ["a", 89.49], ["lot", 89.52], ["like", 89.76], ["it", 89.99], ["grey", 90.41], ["cratered", 91.03], ["no", 91.81], ["air", 92.02]]}, {"s": 92.58, "e": 98.31, "t": "Put it where the Moon is, and at first, you might not even notice. It's a slightly bigger, slightly brighter Moon.", "w": [["put", 92.58], ["it", 92.74], ["where", 92.81], ["the", 92.95], ["moon", 93.03], ["is", 93.31], ["and", 93.75], ["at", 93.85], ["first", 93.93], ["you", 94.37], ["might", 94.53], ["not", 94.75], ["even", 94.9], ["notice", 95.09], ["it's", 95.83], ["a", 95.95], ["slightly", 95.99], ["bigger", 96.51], ["slightly", 96.95], ["brighter", 97.49], ["moon", 97.96]]}, {"s": 98.53, "e": 109.2, "t": "But Mercury is mostly iron. It's four and a half times heavier than the Moon. So its pull on the oceans is four and a half times stronger. Every beach you know would sit underwater at high tide.", "w": [["but", 98.53], ["mercury", 98.69], ["is", 99.26], 