ometers long, would stretch across Mars wider than the whole Moon looks today.", "w": [["but", 123.49], ["here's", 123.87], ["the", 124.15], ["strange", 124.21], ["part", 124.67], ["you", 125.19], ["could", 125.3], ["see", 125.44], ["its", 125.66], ["geography", 125.8], ["without", 126.43], ["a", 126.95], ["telescope", 127.0], ["olympus", 127.92], ["mons", 128.34], ["the", 128.83], ["biggest", 129.04], ["volcano", 129.55], ["in", 130.08], ["the", 130.14], ["solar", 130.21], ["system", 130.52], ["would", 131.12], ["be", 131.25], ["a", 131.4], ["dark", 131.45], ["dot", 131.88], ["you", 132.2], ["could", 132.31], ["spot", 132.44], ["with", 132.78], ["your", 132.9], ["eyes", 133.06], ["and", 133.73], ["valles", 133.89], ["marineris", 134.29], ["a", 135.15], ["canyon", 135.2], ["four", 135.65], ["thousand", 136.03], ["kilometers", 136.55], ["long", 137.08], ["would", 137.68], ["stretch", 137.78], ["across", 138.19], ["mars", 138.55], ["wider", 138.88], ["than", 139.33], ["the", 139.46], ["whole", 139.53], ["moon", 139.9], ["looks", 140.22], ["today", 140.48]]}, {"s": 141.15, "e": 147.22, "t": "Its pull on the oceans? About nine times stronger than the Moon's. Coastal cities would flood with every tide.", "w": [["its", 141.15], ["pull", 141.28], ["on", 141.5], ["the", 141.61], ["oceans", 141.75], ["about", 142.46], ["nine", 142.71], ["times", 143.14], ["stronger", 143.47], ["than", 144.0], ["the", 144.12], ["moon's", 144.18], ["coastal", 144.86], ["cities", 145.27], ["would", 145.68], ["flood", 145.78], ["with", 146.29], ["every", 146.54], ["tide", 146.83]]}, {"s": 147.68, "e": 153.98, "t": "Mars is about the size you'd expect. The next planet is almost Earth's twin, and it would turn your nights into day.", "w": [["mars", 147.68], ["is", 148.03], ["about", 148.13], ["the", 148.47], ["size", 148.54], ["you'd", 148.87], ["expect", 148.96], ["the", 149.72], ["next", 149.82], ["planet", 150.08], ["is", 150.46], ["almost", 150.63], ["earth's", 151.21], ["twin", 151.49], ["and", 152.15], ["it", 152.27], ["would", 152.33], ["turn", 152.47], ["your", 152.68], ["nights", 152.81], ["into", 153.3], ["day", 153.61]]}, {"s": 154.43, "e": 162.72, "t": "Venus. Almost as big as Earth, three and a half times wider than the Moon, and wrapped in bright white clouds that reflect most of the sunlight that hits them.", "w": [["venus", 154.43], ["almost", 155.32], ["as", 155.69], ["big", 155.8], ["as", 156.0], ["earth", 156.14], ["three", 156.69], ["and", 157.0], ["a", 157.09], ["half", 157.12], ["times", 157.36], ["wider", 157.67], ["than", 158.09], ["the", 158.23], ["moon", 158.29], ["and", 158.72], ["wrapped", 159.07], ["in", 159.44], ["bright", 159.58], ["white", 159.97], ["clouds", 160.27], ["that", 160.76], ["reflect", 160.87], ["most", 161.25], ["of", 161.58], ["the", 161.66], ["sunlight", 161.73], ["that", 162.19], ["hits", 162.31], ["them", 162.53]]}, {"s": 162.97, "e": 169.67, "t": "Put it in the Moon's place, and a full Venus would shine about seventy times brighter than a full Moon. You could read a book at midnight.", "w": [["put", 162.97], ["it", 163.14], ["in", 163.23], ["the", 163.31], ["moon's", 163.39], ["place", 163.72], ["and", 164.25], ["a", 164.34], ["full", 164.39], ["venus", 164.83], ["would", 165.21], ["shine", 165.34], ["about", 165.67], ["seventy", 165.9], ["times", 166.43], ["brighter", 166.79], ["than", 167.21], ["a", 167.33], ["full", 167.38], ["moon", 167.7], ["you", 168.32], ["could", 168.41], ["read", 168.54], ["a", 168.69], ["book", 168.73], ["at", 169.06], ["midnight", 169.15]]}, {"s": 169.68, "e": 187.48, "t": "But the real problem isn't the light. It's the weight. Venus is sixty-six times heavier than the Moon. Today, the tide in the open ocean rises about half a meter. With Venus up there, it would rise around thirty. Twice a day. Every port, every beach, every coastal city on Earth... gone.", "w": [["but", 169.68], ["the", 170.04], ["real", 170.11], ["problem", 170.4], ["isn't", 170.82], ["the", 171.12], ["light", 1